{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00136",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.68,
      "end_seconds": 4.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Doctor, we're ready in room two, I've already taken the observations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.62,
      "end_seconds": 9.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.39,
      "end_seconds": 13.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "I've been dealing with my heart racing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.88,
      "end_seconds": 16.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.38,
      "end_seconds": 24.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.88,
      "text": "I'm not sure when it began, to be honest. Some weeks ago, but I can't say how many."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.76,
      "end_seconds": 34.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.3,
      "end_seconds": 43.56,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "I'd say a few times a day. Moderate, I'd say. And I've been feeling hot and sweaty as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.47,
      "end_seconds": 50.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Have you been losing weight even though you're eating well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.06,
      "end_seconds": 65.47,
      "duration_seconds": 14.41,
      "text": "Yes, I have. Oh, and shaky hands. That's been about the same, two weeks. As for shaky hands, pretty moderate, if I'm being honest. Honestly, a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.33,
      "end_seconds": 71.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any diarrhoea, lump in the neck or trouble sleeping?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.27,
      "end_seconds": 77.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "Hmm, no, no diarrhoea, lump in the neck or trouble sleeping."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.8,
      "end_seconds": 81.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "And shortness of breath, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.07,
      "end_seconds": 86.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "No, no shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.23,
      "end_seconds": 89.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.1,
      "end_seconds": 91.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.88,
      "end_seconds": 96.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.34,
      "end_seconds": 106.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.09,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 110.09,
      "end_seconds": 115.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temperature 36.6, BP is 117 over 88, heart rate 118."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.71,
      "end_seconds": 123.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.06,
      "end_seconds": 129.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Yes, high cholesterol. I've had depression for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.17,
      "end_seconds": 136.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known depression. We'll keep that in mind today. Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.46,
      "end_seconds": 139.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "No, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.95,
      "end_seconds": 145.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.96,
      "end_seconds": 160.45,
      "duration_seconds": 13.49,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.25,
      "end_seconds": 167.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.54,
      "end_seconds": 172.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "My uncle had colon cancer. My father was diabetic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.59,
      "end_seconds": 174.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "So, and alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.67,
      "end_seconds": 177.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "I don't drink at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.76,
      "end_seconds": 183.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.93,
      "end_seconds": 189.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Oh, I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.89,
      "end_seconds": 193.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "So, what medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.46,
      "end_seconds": 204.78,
      "duration_seconds": 10.32,
      "text": "I take atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I'm on sertraline, 50 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 205.12,
      "end_seconds": 209.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 25 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.65,
      "end_seconds": 213.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.14,
      "end_seconds": 217.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "No, I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.31,
      "end_seconds": 234.32,
      "duration_seconds": 15.01,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.0,
      "end_seconds": 237.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Right, thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.46,
      "end_seconds": 244.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.67,
      "end_seconds": 247.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Yes, codeine, it gives me vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.96,
      "end_seconds": 252.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.93,
      "end_seconds": 255.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.86,
      "end_seconds": 258.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.78,
      "end_seconds": 276.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Your thyroid feels a little enlarged and smooth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.26,
      "end_seconds": 277.96,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.07,
      "end_seconds": 280.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Open wide for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.46,
      "end_seconds": 304.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "There's a fine tremor in the outstretched hands, and your palms are warm and moist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.42,
      "end_seconds": 305.12,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.54,
      "end_seconds": 333.86,
      "duration_seconds": 25.32,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Okay, so my impression is this: I think we're dealing with an overactive thyroid at this stage. I'd also keep anxiety in mind. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had your heart racing, moderate, and no diarrhoea or lump in the neck."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.3,
      "end_seconds": 335.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.15,
      "end_seconds": 339.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.44,
      "end_seconds": 343.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.43,
      "end_seconds": 355.41,
      "duration_seconds": 10.98,
      "text": "We should do a thyroid scan for hyperthyroidism. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'm going to order a thyroid test, for hyperthyroid symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 355.97,
      "end_seconds": 358.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "We've already done an ECG this morning, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.76,
      "end_seconds": 371.81,
      "duration_seconds": 12.05,
      "text": "Okay, thanks, I'll look at that. Let's use propranolol, 20 milligrams, twice a day, until we review. It's for palpitations and tremor. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.28,
      "end_seconds": 374.2,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.58,
      "end_seconds": 385.62,
      "duration_seconds": 11.04,
      "text": "Limit tea, coffee and anything that speeds up the heart for now. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.16,
      "end_seconds": 393.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "Mm. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 393.85,
      "end_seconds": 395.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.46,
      "end_seconds": 409.67,
      "duration_seconds": 14.21,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse. I'd like to see you again in two weeks. Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.98,
      "end_seconds": 419.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.68,
      "text": "So, I take the propranolol, 20 milligrams, twice a day and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.69,
      "end_seconds": 428.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Wonderful, I think that's it. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 430.16,
      "end_seconds": 433.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "That's everything I wanted to ask. Thank you."
    }
  ]
}